Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000300>

    Annotations: 
        
            Annotations: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/releases/2.11.0/imports/iao-extracted.omn>
        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "textual entity"@en,
        
            Annotations: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/releases/2.11.0/imports/iao-extracted.omn>
        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "Words, sentences, paragraphs, and the written (non-figure) parts of publications are all textual entities"@en,
        
            Annotations: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/releases/2.11.0/imports/iao-extracted.omn>
        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000123>,
        
            Annotations: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/releases/2.11.0/imports/iao-extracted.omn>
        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A textual entity is a part of a manifestation (FRBR sense), a generically dependent continuant whose concretizations are patterns of glyphs intended to be interpreted as words, formulas, etc."@en,
        
            Annotations: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/releases/2.11.0/imports/iao-extracted.omn>
        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "AR, (IAO call 2009-09-01): a document as a whole is not typically a textual entity, because it has pictures in it - rather there are parts of it that are textual entities. Examples: The title, paragraph 2 sentence 7, etc."@en,
        
            Annotations: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/releases/2.11.0/imports/iao-extracted.omn>
        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "MC, 2009-09-14 (following IAO call 2009-09-01): textual entities live at the FRBR (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Functional_Requirements_for_Bibliographic_Records) manifestation level. Everything is significant: line break, pdf and html versions of same document are different textual entities."@en,
        
            Annotations: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/releases/2.11.0/imports/iao-extracted.omn>
        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> "PERSON: Lawrence Hunter"@en,
        
            Annotations: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/releases/2.11.0/imports/iao-extracted.omn>
        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> "text"@en,
        rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/imports/iao-extracted.owl>,
        
            Annotations: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/releases/2.11.0/imports/iao-extracted.omn>
        rdfs:label "textual entity"@en
    
